# PING PONG

Project made for me to practice using a Python game library called "Pygame",
Additionally I want to move that project and put it onto esp32 as well, I bought one and I want to explore its limits

As of right now, my current priority is "pingpong.py" file, any file related to esp32 in this repository might or will not work.

# GAME

You can move either with W and S or UP or DOWN arrow key.
There are 3 different gamemodes:
1) Player vs Player, you use your W and S key as well as UP and DOWN arrow keys. No, this is not multiplayer so it's best use for whenever someone is at your place.
2) Player vs Bot, In case you would just want to play some very simple ping pong.
3) Bot vs Bot, Made this just for fun, no real use in this one.

# ISSUES

If you catch any issue that is game-breaking, please make a Github issue.

